# 25 October 2026 : ZenRay Meshes ARCHETYPE "car" v1 : construction rules first, then fit to the sheet.
# EN: a car is built on a CANONICAL quad cage whose edge loops sit on the design lines:
#   stations along the length (named): nose, hood_lead, cowl (windshield base), roof_front, roof_rear, deck, tail,
#   plus stations around each axle so the wheel arches are real loops;
#   rows around the half section (named): floor_centre, floor_edge, fender_inner, sill, door_low, belt (shoulder),
#   glass_base, roof_edge, roof_centre; mirrored to a closed ring.
# MEASURE reads the sheet frame (profiles: roof line and underside from the side view, half width from the top view,
# width by height from the front view) and finds the key stations by a piecewise linear fit of the roof line (dynamic
# programming, 6 segments). BUILD makes the cage (all quads, mirror symmetric) and lists the CREASE edges (design
# lines: sill, belt, roof edge, cowl, roof front, deck, nose, tail) for a creased Catmull-Clark subdivision in Houdini.
# Every number lives in PARAMS (rules) or in the measured JSON (instance): the archetype is the definition, the car is
# an instance. FR : la voiture se construit sur une cage canonique dont les boucles suivent les lignes du design.
# Usage: python ArchetypeCar.py <work_dir> <out_prefix>
import sys, os, json
import numpy as np
from PIL import Image
from scipy import ndimage as ndi

